If a patient meets at least 2 opioid-use-disorder-criteria during at most 1 year then the patient has an opioid-use-disorder.
Every often-larger-or-longer-than-intended-opioid-use is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every persistent-desire-or-unsuccessful-attempt-to-control-opioid-use is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every great-time-for-opioid-obtaining-use-or-recovery is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every opioid-craving is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every major-work-school-or-home-role-obligation-failing-recurrent-opioid-use is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every continued-opioid-use-despite-persistent-or-recurrent-opioid-caused-social-or-interpersonal-problems is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every important-social-occupational-or-recreational-activity-reducing-opioid-use is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every physically-hazardous-recurrent-opioid-use is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every continued-opioid-use-despite-known-persistent-or-recurrent-likely-opioid-caused-physical-or-psychological-problems is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every opioid-tolerance-criterion is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
Every opioid-withdrawal-criterion is an opioid-use-disorder-criterion.
If a patient needs a markedly-increased-opioid-amount for an intoxication-or-desired-effect and the patient does not provably take an opioid solely under an appropriate-medical-supervision then the patient meets an opioid-tolerance-criterion.
If a patient has a markedly-diminished-effect-with-continued-same-opioid-amount and the patient does not provably take an opioid solely under an appropriate-medical-supervision then the patient meets an opioid-tolerance-criterion.
If a patient has a characteristic-opioid-withdrawal-syndrome and the patient does not provably take an opioid solely under an appropriate-medical-supervision then the patient meets an opioid-withdrawal-criterion.
If a patient takes an opioid-or-closely-related-substance for a withdrawal-symptom-relief-or-avoidance and the patient does not provably take an opioid solely under an appropriate-medical-supervision then the patient meets an opioid-withdrawal-criterion.
